Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Verification of the manuscript QCLT, version 21", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e37895fb-be6a-435a-b13a-38063c886f2a"],

Cell["\<\
A feedback-driven central limit theorem with q-Gaussian limits: checks of the \
calculations, tables and figures\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"a3c3bac9-d4c8-40c9-9514-f4f6d16f63a5"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook checks the calculations of the manuscript \"A feedback-driven \
central limit theorem with q-Gaussian limits\" (G. B. Bagci and T. Oikonomou) \
and redraws its tables and figures. Equation, section, lemma, table and \
figure numbers are those of the manuscript: Eqs. (II.1)-(II.7) in Sec. II, \
(III.1)-(III.5) in Sec. III, (IV.1)-(IV.7) in Sec. IV, (V.1)-(V.4) in Sec. V, \
(A.1)-(A.10) in Appendix A and (B.1)-(B.2) in Appendix B; Tables I-III; \
Figures 1-3. Checks marked additional concern intermediate quantities that \
the manuscript does not tabulate. Every check prints PASS or FAIL when it is \
evaluated, and Section 11 collects all of them in one table.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003744642357573*^9, 
  4.003744644511512*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5c8ad91e-f8a2-467b-a639-\
112568cf7b89"],

Cell["\<\
How to run: Evaluation > Evaluate Notebook. Sections 0 to 5 and Section 10 \
are symbolic or exact checks and numerical checks on grids; they take a few \
minutes in all. Section 6 simulates the recursion (II.1) with the parameters \
of the manuscript (200000 paths, N = 10000, eleven cases); this takes roughly \
10 to 20 minutes. Set mPaths = 20000 in the first cell of Section 6 for a \
quick run. The random seed is fixed, but the random numbers differ from those \
of the Python simulation used for the manuscript, so the simulated numbers \
agree with the manuscript only within sampling error.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.003744720402966*^9, 
  4.003744727228711*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ef7b6b2e-ecd5-45ec-9a57-\
f983566e9efe"],

Cell["\<\
Status. Sections 0-9 were run in Mathematica by G. B. Bagci, and all checks \
passed. For manuscript version 21 the references in the names of the checks \
and in the comments were changed to the numbering of the manuscript; the code \
of Sections 0-9 is unchanged. Three checks were added at the end of Section 2 \
for the paragraph of Sec. II C on the diffusion behind (II.7), and Section 10 \
(Proposition E, Appendix B) was added. The new checks were run in a Wolfram \
kernel and passed; they have not yet been run in Mathematica.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3ba519dd-99e5-417d-afb2-e4e22ec8f150"],

Cell["\<\
What a check can and cannot show. The algebraic identities are verified \
symbolically or in exact arithmetic. Inequalities that hold for all values of \
the variables are tested on grids; a pass on a grid is a consistency check, \
not a proof. Statements that rest on standard theorems (Kolmogorov and \
Weierstrass theorems, the duality formula for the Wasserstein distance, the \
existence of optimal couplings, dominated convergence, uniqueness for linear \
differential equations) are not reproved; the formulas that the proof derives \
from them are checked.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2f10ea81-2d5a-4f27-8a92-5e55ddd02c26"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
0. Setup: the limit law g_b, the constants and the noise laws\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4067356a-0511-49e2-995d-74e87b9703b0"],

Cell["\<\
Definitions: kappa, sigma, the normalizing constant Z_b in closed form, g_b, \
q(b), a_1, Lambda of (IV.4), C_L of (IV.7).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"be11c185-384b-424a-aa4d-30276638d0ff"],

Cell["results = <||>;", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5e5b8223-0813-44cc-bce1-1c54ca5137c0"],

Cell["\<\
check[name_String, cond_] := Module[{ok = TrueQ[cond]},
   results[name] = ok;
   Row[{Style[If[ok, \"PASS\", \"FAIL\"], Bold, If[ok, Darker[Green], Red]], \
\"   \", name}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4a04cd55-320f-4066-8b7f-e6f747da0c2a"],

Cell["\<\
close[x_, y_, tol_ : 10^-8] := Abs[N[x] - N[y]] <= tol Max[1, Abs[N[y]]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3016b4d4-0f2a-4381-bd0c-c6553e3f2a04"],

Cell["kap[b_] := 1 + 1/(2 b);", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"11021717-67bf-4fbd-9a12-ab11d16e15c8"],

Cell["sig[y_, b_, c_] := Sqrt[c + b y^2];", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"08dd00c4-5a96-413f-90f7-769a2155ce9f"],

Cell["\<\
zz[b_, c_] := If[b > 0, c^(1/2 - kap[b]) Sqrt[Pi/b] Gamma[kap[b] - \
1/2]/Gamma[kap[b]],
   c^(1/2 - kap[b]) Sqrt[-Pi/b] Gamma[1 - kap[b]]/Gamma[3/2 - kap[b]]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"09a9d715-3bfa-432d-9723-f3a76d4ac92e"],

Cell["\<\
gb[y_, b_, c_] := If[b > 0 || y^2 < -c/b, (c + b y^2)^(-kap[b])/zz[b, c], 0];\
\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"92be1aba-fafd-4bf3-8f01-1542cccd6723"],

Cell["qOf[b_] := (1 + 4 b)/(1 + 2 b);", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"83d3bbdd-9c90-4d74-977f-9502b795132e"],

Cell["\<\
a1Of[b_, c_] := Sqrt[c] Gamma[kap[b] - 1] Gamma[kap[b]]/Gamma[kap[b] - 1/2]^2;\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"075f22d4-598f-4980-a9fd-4ab6fd9b9331"],

Cell["lamOf[b_, m3_] := Exp[4 Sqrt[2] b^(3/2) m3 (Zeta[3/2] - 1)];", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f35f4855-569c-441b-aed6-471a764c8f81"],

Cell["clOf[b_, c_, m3_] := a1Of[b, c] m3 (33 + 83 b/2 + 6/b);", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2ae0f26c-1bd6-4381-9d27-a8549c7439a9"],

Cell["atoms[\"rademacher\"] = {{1, 1/2}, {-1, 1/2}};", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f9ffa880-5fa9-422f-93ad-87c654e4df99"],

Cell["atoms[\"two\"] = {{2, 1/5}, {-1/2, 4/5}};", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6da3d2bd-8bb2-4a49-83fc-9531dd07eded"],

Cell["\<\
atoms[\"three\"] = {{-Sqrt[2], 1/4}, {0, 1/2}, {Sqrt[2], 1/4}};\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dce423de-52e7-4b95-a111-4d2c75cb0936"],

Cell["\<\
m3[\"rademacher\"] = 1; m3[\"two\"] = 17/10; m3[\"gauss\"] = 2 Sqrt[2/Pi]; \
m3[\"exp\"] = 12/E - 2;\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a266e0f9-b844-44cd-b730-305cc725d8c2"],

Cell["\<\
colB = RGBColor[0.165, 0.471, 0.839]; colO = RGBColor[0.922, 0.408, 0.204]; \
colA = RGBColor[0.106, 0.686, 0.478];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a753ddad-4525-4ca8-bdee-cee18d884095"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Sec. II A: the statement (Eqs. II.1-II.4 and Table I)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a04b44b0-02d1-4e33-b4ce-4e51ae1655ca"],

Cell["(II.2): the normalising constant and the limit law", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"840fd09b-49a4-4bb1-adc0-4d4a49725ada"],

Cell["\<\
zNum[b_, c_] := If[b > 0, NIntegrate[(c + b y^2)^(-kap[b]), {y, -Infinity, \
Infinity}], NIntegrate[(c + b y^2)^(-kap[b]), {y, -Sqrt[-c/b], Sqrt[-c/b]}]];\
\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ab595ba8-c4cd-42b5-9a42-c850ed8db435"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"(II.2): closed form of Z_b equals the integral of D^(-kappa) (b = \
1/3, 1, 2, -1/4, -1/2, -1; c = 1, 23/10)\",
  And @@ Flatten@Table[close[zz[b, c], Quiet@zNum[b, c], 10^-5], {b, {1/3, 1, \
2, -1/4, -1/2, -1}}, {c, {1, 23/10}}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:=",ExpressionUUID->"04721162-0b62-4d4f-b36e-5fb4bb77a6e8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"(II.2): closed form of Z_b equals the integral of D^(-kappa) (b = 1/3, \
1, 2, -1/4, -1/2, -1; c = 1, 23/10)\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003653232985664*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[18]=",ExpressionUUID->"33d91a11-555e-4f8c-93e3-0b36926ebc51"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["(II.3): the q-Gaussian form", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"316e01fb-348f-4b0c-8f40-639cd70984a2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"(II.3): (1-q) B = -b/c and 1/(1-q) = -kappa, with q = (1+4b)/(1+2b) \
and B = (1+2b)/(2c)\",
  Simplify[(1 - qOf[b]) (1 + 2 b)/(2 c) == -b/c] && Simplify[1/(1 - qOf[b]) \
== -kap[b]]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b321807d-9b05-4fd3-8ada-885de2c6477f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"(II.3): (1-q) B = -b/c and 1/(1-q) = -kappa, with q = (1+4b)/(1+2b) and \
B = (1+2b)/(2c)\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003653233024927*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[19]=",ExpressionUUID->"9338de04-0529-48c2-a79e-f6600b3a9d34"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"(II.3): inverse relation b = (q-1)/(2(2-q))\", Simplify[(qOf[b] - \
1)/(2 (2 - qOf[b])) == b]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e69a7583-ba47-4d3d-8206-38ac0bbb69ce"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"(II.3): inverse relation b = (q-1)/(2(2-q))\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003653233030592*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[20]=",ExpressionUUID->"db4a36cc-881d-4716-aeb4-4eae30b3bb9f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Sec. II A: g_b is proportional to [1-(1-q) B y^2]^(1/(1-q)) (the \
ratio does not depend on y)\",
  And @@ Flatten@Table[With[{q = qOf[b], bq = (1 + 2 b)/(2 c)}, close[gb[y, \
b, c]/(1 - (1 - q) bq y^2)^(1/(1 - q)), gb[0, b, c], 10^-10]],
    {b, {1/3, 1, 2, -1/4, -1/3}}, {c, {1, 23/10}}, {y, {1/5, 1/2, 9/10}}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:=",ExpressionUUID->"45b61abf-2421-4b0b-ada3-fcd630887041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"Sec. II A: g_b is proportional to [1-(1-q) B y^2]^(1/(1-q)) (the ratio \
does not depend on y)\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0036532330553017`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[21]=",ExpressionUUID->"8746d994-1361-4470-9996-a124aa4b55ce"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Sec. II A: for b > 0, g_b is the law of Sqrt[c/(1+b)] T with T a \
Student variable with 1 + 1/b degrees of freedom\",
  And @@ Flatten@Table[close[gb[y, b, c], PDF[StudentTDistribution[0, \
Sqrt[c/(1 + b)], 1 + 1/b], y], 10^-10], {b, {1/3, 1, 2}}, {c, {1, 23/10}}, \
{y, {-7/2, -1, 0, 1/3, 5}}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7d09bbde-1440-48a9-ab7f-d7ca11536486"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"Sec. II A: for b > 0, g_b is the law of Sqrt[c/(1+b)] T with T a \
Student variable with 1 + 1/b degrees of freedom\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0036532330818777`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[22]=",ExpressionUUID->"842922a4-5bb1-4990-b395-4fada9887691"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Sec. II A: for b < 0, g_b is the law of L(2V-1) with V a \
Beta(1/(2|b|), 1/(2|b|)) variable\",
  And @@ Flatten@Table[With[{al = -1/(2 b), el = Sqrt[-c/b]}, close[gb[y, b, \
c], PDF[BetaDistribution[al, al], (y/el + 1)/2]/(2 el), 10^-10]],
    {b, {-1/4, -1/2, -1, -5/2}}, {c, {1, 23/10}}, {y, {-1/2, 0, 1/7, 3/5}}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0da66dd4-1555-4f11-9143-bddbdb2a4fa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"Sec. II A: for b < 0, g_b is the law of L(2V-1) with V a Beta(1/(2|b|), \
1/(2|b|)) variable\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.003653233118783*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[23]=",ExpressionUUID->"4274dbe4-4fd8-44c2-afde-5dbcb54a8ea4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
check[\"Table I: q(-1/4) = 0, q(1/3) = 7/5, q(1) = 5/3, q(2) = 9/5; \
kappa(-1/2) = 0 (uniform); kappa(-1) = 1/2 (arcsine)\",
  qOf[-1/4] == 0 && qOf[1/3] == 7/5 && qOf[1] == 5/3 && qOf[2] == 9/5 && \
kap[-1/2] == 0 && kap[-1] == 1/2]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:=",ExpressionUUID->"dd42be9b-9f3f-4cde-813a-524d1b0fbd2a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   StyleBox["\"PASS\"", Bold, 
    RGBColor[0, 
     Rational[2, 3], 0], StripOnInput -> False], "\"   \"", 
   "\"Table I: q(-1/4) = 0, q(1/3) = 7/5, q(1) = 5/3, q(2) = 9/5; kappa(-1/2) \
= 0 (uniform); kappa(-1) = 1/2 (arcsine)\""},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0036532331237392`*^9},
